  "synonym_discrimination": {
    "words": [
      "injury-n",
      "wound-n",
      "damage-n"
    ],
    "note": "**Injury** is harm to the body, usually from an accident or sport: *a knee injury*. A **wound** is an injury in which the skin is cut or broken, especially by a weapon: *a knife wound*. **Damage** is used mostly for harm to things (*damage to the car*); for people it appears mainly in medical use for harm to an organ (*brain damage*), not for an ordinary injury."
  },
  "usage_note": null,
