      "incorrect": "He had a damage to his leg.",
      "correct": "He had an injury to his leg.",
      "note": "For ordinary harm to the body from an accident, use **injury**; **damage** is used mostly for things."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "She got injury in the game.",
      "correct": "She was injured in the game.",
      "note": "Use the verb in the passive (**be injured**), or say **she got an injury**."
